WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.120
Rose Tico fans can claim a victory, well,
sort of.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.780
An alleged summary of the Star Wars: The Rise
of Skywalker script has emerged on YouTube

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.340
from a former professional screenplay reader
named Robert Burnett.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.440
This supposed version of the script is said
to have been written during Colin Trevorrow's

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:22.110
time in the director's chair, before he lost
his job in 2017 and the entire project started

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.960
over with The Force Awakens director J.J.
Abrams back at the helm.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.480
This script, with the working title The Duel
of the Fates, appears to be a profoundly different

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:35.360
movie from the one we received in December
2019, though several of the individual concepts

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.240
are similar enough that they might have been
repurposed for The Rise of Skywalker.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.420
The story itself, however, is entirely different,
and Kelly Marie Tran's Rose Tico is at its

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:44.960
core.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.480
"I work behind pipes all day.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.200
Doing talking with resistance heroes is not
my forte.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:51.620
I'm Rose."

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.140
Fans of Rose, who was introduced in The Last
Jedi, have been upset by how The Rise of Skywalker

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:02.570
minimized her presence and insulted the character,
on top of the real-life harassment Tran experienced

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.620
on social media because of her role.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.530
They can perhaps find some bittersweet comfort
in the possibility that, somewhere along the

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:10.860
line, someone might have cared about Rose.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:16.260
However, we can't 100% guarantee that the
alleged script described in the video is genuine.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.210
Burnett explains straight away that he won't
provide proof of the script beyond cropped

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:24.810
images of the title page and the original
narration crawl, or any detail as to how he

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:28.760
got a hold of it, but if you want to imagine
this is legit, hey, go for it.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:32.820
Let's take a look at the version of Rose Tico
in The Rise of Skywalker that might have been.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:37.100
This alleged original Rise of Skywalker script
actually opens on Rose Tico and BB-8.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:42.610
A good chunk of the first act has her attempting,
along with Finn, Poe, and eventually Rey,

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:47.940
to sabotage the transportation of ore used
for building Star Destroyers at the Kuat Shipyards.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:53.030
Long story short, the sabotage goes very poorly
for our heroes, but with luck, they escape

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:57.630
(are you ready for this?) by jacking an entire
freaking Star Destroyer off the lot and peeling

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.500
out of the shipyards at lightspeed.

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:04.160
All the while, Rose is described as being
front and center, doing her best to reorganize

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:06.800
when plans A, B, and Z all fail.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.430
There are two major teams performing missions
in this alleged script: Rey, Poe, and Chewbacca

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:17.359
take off on their own to do their half, while
Rose, Finn, C3PO, and R2-D2 depart for Coruscant

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.720
to try a desperate gamble.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.379
In trying to snuff out the Resistance for
good, the First Order has choked off all intersystem

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.040
communication at its source.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.800
Rey learns from the texts she picked up in
The Last Jedi, however, that the Jedi Temple

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:33.500
houses a giant kyber crystal that the Old
Republic used thousands of years ago as a

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.109
communication system the First Order doesn't
have the means to control.

00:02:37.109 --> 00:02:41.279
Lighting this ancient beacon is the last hope
of the Resistance to gather allies, and Rose

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.320
takes point on this do-or-die mission.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.200
Once the beacon subplot is completed on Coruscant,
the alleged Rise of Skywalker script continues

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.680
on into the city itself.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:54.040
Since the fall of the Republic as we knew
it in the Star Wars prequel trilogy, the city-planet

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.680
has taken a major hit, with most citizens
falling into scavenging and homelessness.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:03.120
Rose and Finn navigate this underclass and
eventually help incite a revolt.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.999
You heard that right: the woman who lost the
only family she had left in a civil war gets

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:12.500
to assist inciting the biggest on-screen popular
revolt against fascism in Star Wars, in Coruscant.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:13.560
Quite a climax.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.980
This all takes place while a massive battle
occurs in orbit over Coruscant, with General

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:20.849
Leia's forces united by Lando Calrissian.

00:03:20.849 --> 00:03:24.730
The cherry on top is mentioned in passing
by Burnett as he wraps up the video: Once

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:28.799
the First Order is defeated, the remaining
leadership attempt to flee from Coruscant

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:30.639
in a giant mobile headquarters.

00:03:30.639 --> 00:03:34.569
At some point in the story that Burnett doesn't
describe, Rose messes with the compound's

00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:38.849
navigation computers and when the complex
goes to lightspeed, the travel vectors are

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:42.440
incorrect and it crashes into a planet, destroying
the Order for good.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:46.860
It's not as elegant as a one-in-a-million
shot into an exhaust port, but that is wicked

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.360
cool.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.280
Sadly, since there's no proof that any of
that is actually true, you're gonna have to

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.880
take it with a grain of salt.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.119
In fact, though it might have existed at one
point, fans of Rose might rather pretend the

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.440
screenplay draft didn't.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.540
After all, all it would be is a reminder of
something they got cheated out of.

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:06.579
The past three years have been tumultuous
for the Star Wars franchise between the backlash

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:11.329
over The Last Jedi and failure of Solo, and
Trevorrow's professional merit seemed to have

00:04:11.329 --> 00:04:14.900
dropped after his film Book of Henry utterly
bombed at the box office.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:18.620
Being the poster boy for the biggest franchise
on Earth must have been a lot of pressure

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:22.770
at the time, and it appears that maybe in
the end, a bunch of fallible humans cracked

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:23.580
underneath it.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.820
Despite the mixed overall response to The
Rise of Skywalker, many people did in fact

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:32.260
enjoy it, and that's the legacy of Star Wars
as a whole: it's too many things to too many

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.680
people, and there's no way in hell it could
ever please everybody.

